{:edb/db-before-t 1927 :edb/db-after-t 1928 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535240 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:13:33.006Z" 13194139535240 true] [17592186105819 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339273 13194139535240 true] [17592186105819 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339280 13194139535240 true] [17592186105820 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339287 13194139535240 true] [17592186105993 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/e2ab6906100a96a123b4b1520613f1e38fe2c7e77af390a8efe0596a2861727d.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535240 false] [17592186105993 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/e2ab6906100a96a123b4b1520613f1e38fe2c7e77af390a8efe0596a2861727d.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535240 true] [17592186106472 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535240 true] [17592186106472 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/131d9f30fac5b1cc4b8eb72a989ca16b0d3cbf7d16725aa38581bfd115b1fc77.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535240 true] [17592186106472 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1351/Source/Images/q-96873.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T$?" 13194139535240 false] [17592186106472 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(1,-2)$, $(-1,2),$ $(-4,8).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/87d2a7f522d68e1a50d9c5bb5e33498b2a28e869785f5109c4f6bf3a1c7ff701.png)" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339273 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339274 13194139535240 true] [17592186339273 1089 "q-147561" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339273 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535240 true] [17592186339273 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/d88ae8667df81624f0a28295c980f846ae88e9b4766fe0d0f692dd75509a56e9.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339273 1113 #uuid "de2d7c97-764c-58c0-b8ba-f8d09c210ae1" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339273 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 20 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(1,4)$, $(5,20)$, and  $(2,8).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/94247512fd446447144d808c76d00bc9c0d50d4175697597360117eca00b3cf1.png)" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339275 13194139535240 true] [17592186339274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339276 13194139535240 true] [17592186339274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339277 13194139535240 true] [17592186339274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339278 13194139535240 true] [17592186339274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339279 13194139535240 true] [17592186339274 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535240 true] [17592186339274 1041 "selection" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339274 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339275 13194139535240 true] [17592186339274 1110 #uuid "94dd94f9-a34d-504b-a190-d7ad674ef9ae" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339275 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/94247512fd446447144d808c76d00bc9c0d50d4175697597360117eca00b3cf1.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339275 1111 #uuid "6fc35e15-010d-5c1c-a2b8-a51fad741f64" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339276 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/57bedcb6a7191770472af16526b2172ad0c8da718de33b606bc168c514a367d8.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339276 1111 #uuid "75adcf9e-815d-57a1-887d-20ffd3892bab" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339277 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/aefad4c0112e05c1a014ab7a6c684207d047971eccff5fc1b1a637b7d09d8e94.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339277 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339277 1111 #uuid "d1e3c743-cfa3-5cc0-a1c7-9b4575fbab2e" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339278 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/fc9a40db16e8434cadb89266518dcf56c6ed60213ecde42d237229466cdd99d0.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339278 1111 #uuid "397aa031-151c-5547-82fb-185687a4d390" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339279 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/12850dda11d88566b9f62cb9a3d91b79c2b32900c76280257aae14aa69375ef9.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339279 1111 #uuid "3b9a074c-6f79-53eb-9290-67e60175eb82" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339280 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339281 13194139535240 true] [17592186339280 1089 "q-147605" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339280 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535240 true] [17592186339280 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/add078cb1b05f772f25c91a4736f5aacd4490ff8556ce6a0d0ea7ad44869d0e7.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339280 1113 #uuid "873c9a2b-8c1b-5842-a449-297472752d44" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339280 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 10 & 0 & -20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-2,10)$, $(0,0),$ $(4,-20).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/8c86cb108725b3f1c7b5731dda0f11a5cb21a7daa023c5153cce1ece3ba6ba0f.png)" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339282 13194139535240 true] [17592186339281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339283 13194139535240 true] [17592186339281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339284 13194139535240 true] [17592186339281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339285 13194139535240 true] [17592186339281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339286 13194139535240 true] [17592186339281 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535240 true] [17592186339281 1041 "selection" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339281 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339285 13194139535240 true] [17592186339281 1110 #uuid "156c3aba-8995-5b5c-b49c-308998a55d7a" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339282 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/5e316ceff92e78155ee352a2e5c3c526d30852fb1803fd9cfb938bea3e5cf984.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339282 1111 #uuid "6e4a8430-6b20-5a38-879f-aed55131dec6" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339283 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/dfa05a8c2c943d5f74e5e5fef468006117c97b2d3d0a7b7a6b9c2024b6089272.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339283 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339283 1111 #uuid "ee0afb26-d708-5013-83f4-7d011a687b0b" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339284 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/d3f815e4205f0a24a125162072843fe507d0683ce40a89fdd13ee29c296f7500.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339284 1111 #uuid "00397b04-978a-5183-bc58-165cbe505603" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339285 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/b6fe02d5b3d96aeaa6a4edc9a027ec69993330252322e10a57618dd499bb02b5.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339285 1111 #uuid "2aa6565e-339f-5618-9b98-de9e108cd1e9" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339286 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/6ba878568654dc85dba3ac561617132f851e62b63473eb8239fa716f53cd0dcd.png" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535240 true] [17592186339286 1111 #uuid "d91a02e3-6aaa-5ee7-864a-e5b3a2781b4b" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339287 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339288 13194139535240 true] [17592186339287 1089 "q-162204" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339287 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535240 true] [17592186339287 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/2cb5cf6d3307c1291dbbb785cd71ed6edecba3d448afbc2f5f5c2d1128b457c1.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339287 1113 #uuid "2ebf302f-e626-5c64-a0a0-339c0907c8f2" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339287 1145 "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 6-(-4)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a singular nonzero matrix. Therefore, the image of the quadrilateral under the action of $T$ is a line segment." 13194139535240 true] [17592186339288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339289 13194139535240 true] [17592186339288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339290 13194139535240 true] [17592186339288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339291 13194139535240 true] [17592186339288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339292 13194139535240 true] [17592186339288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339293 13194139535240 true] [17592186339288 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535240 true] [17592186339288 1041 "selection" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339288 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339291 13194139535240 true] [17592186339288 1110 #uuid "b4b2c88e-6c1e-5b13-ad87-12bf23911a60" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339289 1034 "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535240 true] [17592186339289 1111 #uuid "876b4bd5-718d-5deb-9d7e-2d10440aca4e" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339290 1034 "A triangle" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535240 true] [17592186339290 1111 #uuid "c1114dec-3774-5e74-9ef0-1c064c926d9c" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339291 1034 "A line segment" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535240 true] [17592186339291 1111 #uuid "d14ed35a-8d21-5643-bb24-7ac6b5632bba" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339292 1034 "A quadrilateral" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535240 true] [17592186339292 1111 #uuid "2bb68096-50a5-5fda-942e-4abd37aa54f1" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339293 1034 "A point, different from the origin" 13194139535240 true] [17592186339293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535240 true] [17592186339293 1111 #uuid "62696a8e-2598-5fc7-b61e-1fa63b4062fa" 13194139535240 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-147561" 17592186339273 "q-147561/selection" 17592186339274 "q-147561/selection/2a99950d9f52e6b3da0a8e93fdfa2a629d20bdd783d91ac0324b25a74b7479f3" 17592186339275 "q-147561/selection/77a692b7a23b5c33786b0b15d0c73a37333a73cffbc7ff50a590caba3131dccd" 17592186339276 "q-147561/selection/80fc8607cc1d95f2850c2ba87e9c863a70e6efd53a2622806715c11d10d18001" 17592186339277 "q-147561/selection/93db2764c9625fa0ae3c5330cdbc43fa0c5cb396b33f47ae3d231050f1d27753" 17592186339278 "q-147561/selection/c968cdb055130ac9d7d194d1986856a77d954e1826e3586b81b53fe81d84078a" 17592186339279 "q-147605" 17592186339280 "q-147605/selection" 17592186339281 "q-147605/selection/2f2861cd5c80f773961e0afe6308e4e7218d9a13b6ab6aec7b02642cf1484c4c" 17592186339282 "q-147605/selection/6e07cb506d55b153e0de10780991bf49c1227e352aee0c66da00d223b668bb18" 17592186339283 "q-147605/selection/791de516b9155996af83ece742226e395497ad7b88efd79e73be51c41c56ce1c" 17592186339284 "q-147605/selection/a018a4227a949b4a360098edb9776f161886918a1eec041313eea5368f959d46" 17592186339285 "q-147605/selection/fde829ee0557c04adb291fe52388620d28cd97c7c581c13f29319fc21de8f430" 17592186339286 "q-162204" 17592186339287 "q-162204/selection" 17592186339288 "q-162204/selection/0f01227ab4132a1cf25abe47ace21e46fc0c901af076ff4c5dae675af9c522e9" 17592186339289 "q-162204/selection/99d5aeb2f87bf6ef13f130429773b8288f79a42bed11813